On July 24, 2023 at approx.0800 hours I, Kellen Nicholls, a radio operator of the Department of Fisheries and Oceans in Langley BC received a phone call stating that on July 21st a report was made to the Radio Room regarding a boat ramp that has been constructed on Crown Land. The caller identified themselves as Patrick Sorfleet, the director of planning and development at the District of Sparwood (250-425-6828). Patrick stated that on July 21st, 2023 one of their bylaw staff was notified of the boat ramp and forwarded the information to the radio room, but due to unforseen reasons at this point in time, no report was made. According to the caller, the ramp has been built leading into the Elk River, on crown land. No further information was provided by the caller at this time.
