July 6, 2023 @ 8:45 am
Fish salvage incidental mortality - 1 Western Terrestrial Garter snake found dead in a minnow trap (40 cm long) 
Traps in area were set at .75 to 1 m depth, work was overseen by qualified biologists. Multiple QPs were consulted and traps remain set in the pond for the last day of fish salvage effort. Traps to be pulled on Friday July 7th.

Teck reports all mortalities discovered on site. I called the RAPP number to report but felt that this incident did not meet any of the listed options. I am hoping you will be able to follow up with a short email so I can close the loop on our reporting. 
