Yesterday, July 4 at 6:15, my domestic cat bolted into the house as though her tail was on fire, and ran upstairs and hid under a bed; this was the most frightened I have ever seen her. I looked out through all my windows and found a young cougar cub at my back door; it did not seem relaxed or comfortable, and the mother was not in sight. I opened and slammed the door, and the cub ran off.
Half an hour later, I observed an adult probably female cougar in my pasture coming towards my house, I imagine returning from an unsuccessful hunt. When she saw me on my balcony, she stopped and stared, then proceeded in a less relaxed fashion to the woods that go around the back of my house. I did not yell at her; I wanted her to reconnect with the cub.
I advised my neighbours who have toddlers, sheep and poultry. They didn’t see the cougar and had no losses. I have chickens and also had no losses.
We did not see a cougar today.

