Today the doe charged at their dog.  Debby tried to scare the doe away and was met with snorting and stomping.  Debby grabbed a walking stick to scare her and the doe charged. Debby retreated to the house but continued to yell and blasted her air horn, hoping to startle her and convince her to move on. When Debby got back outside the doe was closer to the house trying to get the dog. Debby blasted the air horn and the doe stopped, whistle snorted, stamped and acted like she was going to charge.  Debby then stomped and let off the air horn again and the doe backed off and she was able to get the dog inside.

Concerned that the doe is not deterred by them at all and worried they or the dog may be attacked. Appreciate that the doe may have a fawn somewhere but too unpredictable with little ones around. ',null,null,null,null,null,null,'Crescent Valley, BC','Krestova Road','2023-07-11','15:20:00','2023-07-12 15:20:03',null,'TBTHIN@idir','2023-07-16 13:12:05',null,null,null,null,'OPEN','CRSNTVLY',ST_GeomFromText('POINT(-117.5511111 49.4497222)')) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
